                                                   EXPERIMENT 1.1 Contains Duplicate(217)
                                                  
AIM: Given an integer array nums, return true if any value appears at least twice in the array, and return false if every element is distinct.

ALGORITHM:
i) Take the input array nums.

ii) Sort the array in ascending order using nums.sort().

iii) Traverse the sorted array from index 1 to len(nums) - 1.

iv) For each index i, compare the current element nums[i] with the previous element nums[i - 1].

v) If nums[i] == nums[i - 1], it means a duplicate element is found.

vi) Return True immediately.

vii) If the loop finishes without finding any duplicate, return False.

CODE:
class Solution:
    def containsDuplicate(self, nums: List[int]) -> bool:
        nums.sort()

        for i in range(1,len(nums)):
            if nums[i]==nums[i-1]:
                return True
        return False


                                                   EXPERIMENT 1.2 Contains Duplicate(II)(219)

AIM: Given an integer array nums, return true if any value appears at least twice in the array, and return false if every element is distinct.

ALGORITHM: 
i) Take the input array nums and integer k.

ii) Create an empty dictionary seen to store each element and its latest index.

iii) Traverse the array from index 0 to len(nums) - 1.

iv) For each element nums[i], check if it already exists in the dictionary seen.

v) If it exists, calculate the distance between the current index and the previous index: i - seen[nums[i]]

vi) If the distance is less than or equal to k, return True because a nearby duplicate is found.

vii) Update the dictionary with the current index: seen[nums[i]] = i.This ensures the dictionary always stores the most recent occurrence of the element.

viii) Repeat Steps 5–8 until all elements are checked.

ix) If no nearby duplicate is found after traversing the entire array, return False.

CODE:
class Solution:
    def containsNearbyDuplicate(self, nums: List[int], k: int) -> bool:
        seen={}
        for i in range (len(nums)):
            if nums[i] in seen:
                if i-seen[nums[i]]<=k:
                    return True

            seen[nums[i]]=i

        return False
        
